import json,re
p1=json.load(open('part1.json')); ALL=p1['ALL']
cl=json.load(open('part2.json'))+json.load(open('part3.json'))
for x in cl:
    x['result']=x['result'].replace("nine files that use transient storage say ^0.8.24 and 36 files say ^0.8.0","nine files say ^0.8.24 and 36 files say ^0.8.0").replace("src/interfaces/IPoolManager.sol:166-171","src/interfaces/IPoolManager.sol:165-171")
leads=[
 {"chainIds":ALL,"lens":"L5","question":"OpenZeppelin M-03 is left to the periphery. Do the deployed PositionManagers (the 23,877 byte build on 19 networks and the 19,965 byte build on HyperEVM and Elysium) reject a mint or an increase when the pool price makes the amounts exceed the caller's maxima, and do the published SDK and the launch pad hooks with most pools pass maxima that bind?","why":"Core accepts any starting price from any account and moves the price of an empty pool for free (src/PoolManager.sol:117-134, src/libraries/Pool.sol:344-437). If a widely used path adds first liquidity without a binding bound, an ordinary account can take part of that deposit on every network.","priority":"medium"},
 {"chainIds":[42220,7777777],"lens":"L3","question":"Celo and Zora have an address that reports the PoolManager's native balance and no protocol fee controller. When the owner sets a controller there, is its collect function open to any account as on the eight networks that have one, and does a native fee collection then run while the face is synced?","why":"The synced currency check in collectProtocolFees skips address(0) (src/ProtocolFees.sol:49). On Optimism, Polygon and Arc that already lets a native collection lower the face balance between sync and settle. Celo is the one network where the face can also be paid out by take, so the walk should be repeated there once a controller exists.","priority":"low"},
 {"chainIds":ALL,"lens":"L5","question":"Which behaviour is the build for the 21 deployments meant to have: the lock check that src/interfaces/IProtocolFees.sol:40 and the Trail of Bits fix review describe, or the synced currency check that src/ProtocolFees.sol:49-52 and test/PoolManager.t.sol:1001-1039 pin? If the lock check returns, which tests and which of the eight fee adapters change behaviour?","why":"The interface comment, the unused _isUnlocked hook and the audit record say one thing and the source and its tests say another. The ledger judged the present text harmless. A restored lock check would change what F-014 and F-071 describe and would make collection revert whenever it is triggered inside any unlock.","priority":"low"}]
leadResults=[{"leadId":"L-482","outcome":"cleared","answer":"Answered for the OpenZeppelin report, the Trail of Bits report and the hook permissions note. The other three reports belong to unit core-code-audit-walk-b. I read the two reports and the note page by page and wrote one result for each of the 24 OpenZeppelin findings, the 6 Trail of Bits findings, the 7 code quality items of its appendix C, its invariant tables and static invariants, and the 27 effects of the note. No finding of these documents is open in a way that lets an ordinary account take or lock funds of others. The fix that a report describes is absent from the source in two places: the lock guards of Trail of Bits finding 3 (sync and collectProtocolFees), and noDelegateCall on unlock, take, settle, settleFor, mint and burn from OpenZeppelin CR-01. Both are findings of this file with severity info. For the first I confirmed on the deployed contracts of Optimism, Polygon and Arc that a native fee collection runs inside an unlock while the native face is synced and that only the holder of that sync pays. OpenZeppelin C-01 is closed by src/PoolManager.sol:356 and 285-286, and a walk on all 21 deployed PoolManagers, with the real face on Celo, Arc, Polygon, Optimism and Zora, gave no double credit. OpenZeppelin M-03 and Trail of Bits finding 6 are unresolved by decision of the team and are recorded as low findings. The hook effects are by design and are tied to F-004. Everything on chain was tested against the contracts deployed today, because the checkout cannot be built in this session."}]
out={"unit":"core-code-audit-walk-a","profiles":[],"findings":p1['findings'],"cleared":cl,"leads":leads,"leadResults":leadResults}
json.dump(out,open('../core-code-audit-walk-a.research.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)
# style scan
txt=json.dumps(out,ensure_ascii=False)
for bad in ['—','–','**']:
    print(repr(bad),txt.count(bad))
for w in ['crucial','robust','landscape','highlight','underscore']:
    print(w,len(re.findall(w,txt,re.I)))
print('key as word:',[m.group(0) for m in re.finditer(r'.{25}\bkey\b.{15}',txt,re.I)][:20])
print('not but:',[m.group(0) for m in re.finditer(r'\bnot\b[^.]{0,60}\bbut\b[^.]{0,40}',txt)][:20])
print(len(out['findings']),len(out['cleared']),len(out['leads']))
